      "code_hash": "af801029cd5ab885a53f520667bed78d",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h1 id=\"explore-iron_ore_throughput\">Explore <code>iron_ore_throughput</code></h1>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Guided walkthrough of how FLE <strong>tasks</strong> work \u2014 based on\n<a href=\"../../docs/TASKS_GUIDE.md\"><code>docs/TASKS_GUIDE.md</code></a>.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">You do <strong>not</strong> need an LLM. Each action is a short <strong>Python program</strong> run\ninside Factorio; the reply is mostly <strong>text</strong> (<code>raw_text</code>) plus a reward.</span>\n<div class=\"language-text codehilite\"><pre><span></span><code>goal + inventory + map\n        \u2502\n        \u25bc\n   reset() \u2500\u2500\u25ba write Python \u2500\u2500\u25ba step() \u2500\u2500\u25ba read stdout / reward\n                    \u25b2                            \u2502\n                    \u2514\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500 next program \u25c4\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2518\n</code></pre></div>\n<span class=\"paragraph\"><strong>Tip:</strong> In the notebook footer, set <em>On Cell Change</em> \u2192 <strong>lazy</strong> so live\nFactorio cells only run when you ask.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "vblA",
