    {
      "id": "PKri",
      "code_hash": "635c2b188e13070a25c7c419ff102de1",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h3 id=\"whats-inside-a-task\">What\u2019s inside a task</h3>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">When you later <code>make_env(\"iron_ore_throughput\")</code>, FLE builds:</span>\n<ol>\n<li>A live Factorio instance (Docker / RCON)</li>\n<li>A <strong>task object</strong> (goal, inventory, scoring rule)</li>\n<li>A gym wrapper that turns programs into <code>step()</code> calls</li>\n</ol>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Lab-play starts with a <strong>populated inventory</strong> and <strong>all tech researched</strong>.\nEarly friction is \u201cplace and fuel correctly,\u201d not grinding for a pickaxe.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\"><strong>Scoring (easy to miss):</strong> after each program the task roughly sleeps\n~60 in-game seconds, measures automatic iron-ore throughput, uses that as\n<strong>reward</strong>, and sets <strong>done</strong> when throughput \u2265 16.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">So a program that only prints <code>nearest(Resource.IronOre)</code> often scores\n<code>reward=0.0</code> \u2014 correct; nothing is mining yet.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "Xref",
      "code_hash": "5d32f2a2ba24d7c908011079b357607a",
